# Data Science Guidelines (Python):

<purpose>
Follow all of these guidelines when programming in jupyter notebooks, doing exploratory analyses, and data science
</purpose>

141. **Use `pandas` and `numpy` idiomatically—avoid loops**.
142. **Use vectorized operations for performance**.
143. **Keep notebooks clean—modularize logic in scripts**.
144. **Use environment management (e.g., conda) for reproducibility**.
145. **Track experiments with tools like MLflow or Weights & Biases**.
146. **Use `.loc`/`.iloc` correctly—know the difference**.
147. **Profile memory with `memory_profiler` for large datasets**.
148. **Document data transformations clearly**.
149. **Use `scikit-learn` pipelines for clean modeling workflows**.
150. **Export models using `joblib`, `pickle`, or ONNX responsibly**.
